  "metric_views": [
    {
      "view_name": "procurement_metrics",
      "source_table": "procurement_orders",
      "dimensions": [
        {
          "name": "order_date",
          "expr": "order_date"
        },
        {
          "name": "material_class",
          "expr": "material_class"
        },
        {
          "name": "supplier_region",
          "expr": "supplier_region"
        },
        {
          "name": "delivery_status",
          "expr": "delivery_status"
        }
      ],
      "measures": [
        {
          "name": "total_order_value",
          "expr": "SUM(order_quantity_kg * unit_cost_usd_kg)",
          "comment": "Total procurement value USD"
        },
        {
          "name": "total_order_quantity_kg",
          "expr": "SUM(order_quantity_kg)",
          "comment": "Total ordered quantity in kg"
        },
        {
          "name": "avg_lead_time_weeks",
          "expr": "AVG(lead_time_weeks)",
          "comment": "Average quoted lead time in weeks"
        },
        {
          "name": "total_po_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT po_id)",
          "comment": "Total purchase orders"
        },
        {
          "name": "late_delivery_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN delivery_status = 'Late' THEN po_id END)",
          "comment": "Number of late deliveries"
        },
        {
          "name": "unique_material_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT material_id)",
          "comment": "Number of distinct materials"
        },
        {
          "name": "max_order_quantity_kg",
          "expr": "MAX(order_quantity_kg)",
          "comment": "Maximum order quantity kg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "view_name": "supply_position_metrics",
      "source_table": "supply_snapshots",
      "dimensions": [
        {
          "name": "snapshot_date",
          "expr": "snapshot_date"
        },
        {
          "name": "material_class",
          "expr": "material_class"
        },
        {
          "name": "at_risk_flag",
          "expr": "at_risk_flag"
        }
      ],
      "measures": [
        {
          "name": "total_on_hand_kg",
          "expr": "SUM(on_hand_kg)",
          "comment": "Total on-hand inventory in kg"
        },
        {
          "name": "avg_days_of_supply",
          "expr": "AVG(days_of_supply)",
          "comment": "Average days of supply"
        },
        {
          "name": "critical_material_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN at_risk_flag = 'Critical' THEN material_id END)",
          "comment": "Number of materials in critical supply"
        },
        {
          "name": "total_committed_kg",
          "expr": "SUM(committed_kg)",
          "comment": "Total committed inventory in kg"
        },
        {
          "name": "snapshot_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT snapshot_id)",
          "comment": "Total snapshots"
        },
        {
          "name": "total_safety_stock_kg",
          "expr": "SUM(safety_stock_kg)",
          "comment": "Total safety stock kg"
        },
        {
          "name": "max_on_hand_kg",
          "expr": "MAX(on_hand_kg)",
          "comment": "Maximum on hand kg"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports long-lead materials planning for an aerospace OEM/Tier-1 sourcing 20 critical materials (titanium, nickel superalloys, carbon fiber, aluminum, specialty steel, ceramic matrix composites) across 6 supplier regions (North America, Europe, Japan, China, South Korea, Australia). Stakeholders include Procurement Managers (PO performance, late delivery), VP Supply Chain (OTD, supplier quality, single-source risk), and COO (at-risk materials, production stoppage).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Supplier OTD % target >95%; industry benchmark 90-95%; tracked via late_delivery_count / total_po_count\n- Days of supply = avg_days_of_supply; production materials target 30-60 days, long-lead forgings 90+ days\n- Lead time (weeks) = avg_lead_time_weeks; titanium 30-40, composites 16-24, forgings 40-60\n- Quality acceptance % target >99% on flight-critical components\n- Critical / at-risk material count = critical_material_count where at_risk_flag = 'At Risk'\n- Monthly spend = total_order_value (USD) — drives material P&L\n- Single-source risk = single_source_flag (count materials with single supplier)\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - procurement_metrics (source: procurement_orders) — dims: order_date, material_class, supplier_region, delivery_status; measures: total_order_value, total_order_quantity_kg, avg_lead_time_weeks, total_po_count, late_delivery_count, unique_material_count, max_order_quantity_kg.\n  - supply_position_metrics (source: supply_snapshots) — dims: snapshot_date, material_class, at_risk_flag; measures: total_on_hand_kg, avg_days_of_supply, critical_material_count, total_committed_kg, snapshot_count, total_safety_stock_kg, max_on_hand_kg.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. material_id, material_name, unit_cost_usd_kg, quality_acceptance, single_source_flag, on_time_delivery_pct).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Top 10 materials by total order value over the last 12 months, and which supplier regions ship them?",
    "Show monthly trend in late delivery count by supplier region.",
    "Which material classes have the lowest days of supply right now, and what is at risk?",
    "Top 10 supplier regions by average lead time in weeks — flag any above industry benchmark.",
    "How has total monthly spend trended over the trailing 12 months by material class?",
    "Which materials are flagged as critical or at-risk this month, and what is on hand?",
    "Show monthly trend in average lead time weeks for the trailing 12 months."
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in unique materials?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT order_date, MEASURE(unique_material_count) AS unique_material_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.procurement_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY order_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has highest order quantity kg changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT order_date, MEASURE(max_order_quantity_kg) AS max_order_quantity_kg",
        "FROM {fqn}.procurement_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY order_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in highest on hand kg?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, MEASURE(max_on_hand_kg) AS max_on_hand_kg",
        "FROM {fqn}.supply_position_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does total order quantity in kilograms break down by material identifier for 'On Time' records?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT material_id, COUNT(*) AS record_count, SUM(order_quantity_kg) AS total_order_quantity_kg",
        "FROM {fqn}.procurement_orders",
        "WHERE delivery_status = 'On Time' GROUP BY material_id ORDER BY total_order_quantity_kg DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total on-hand inventory in kg over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(on_hand_kg) AS total_on_hand_kg",
        "FROM {fqn}.supply_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average supplier on-time delivery rate changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT report_month, AVG(on_time_delivery_pct) AS avg_on_time_delivery_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.supply_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY report_month ORDER BY report_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has late delivery count changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT order_date, MEASURE(late_delivery_count) AS late_delivery_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.procurement_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY order_date"
      ]
    }
  ],
